  "facts": [
    "The Verrazzano–Narrows Bridge, opened November 21, 1964, boasts a 4,260‑foot central span that was the longest suspension bridge span worldwide until 1981, and remains the longest in the Americas.",
    "Designed by Othmar Ammann and colleagues, the double‑deck bridge carries 13 lanes of I‑278—seven upper, six lower—linking Staten Island and Brooklyn and collecting tolls in both directions.",
    "A 2018 correction fixed a 1960 misspelling that had left the bridge officially named \"Verrazano–Narrows Bridge\" for nearly six decades, a clerical error traced back to the original construction contract."
  ],
